# 🔄 Authentication Quick Reference

## Current Setup: Development (Keycloak) 

### ⚡ Quick Switch to Production (Azure AD B2C)

1. **Edit Configuration File**: `src/app/auth/keycloak.config.ts`
   ```typescript
   const isDevelopment = false; // Change from true to false
   ```

2. **Update Azure AD B2C Values**:
   ```typescript
   const azureAdB2CConfig: KeycloakConfig = {
     url: 'https://YOUR_TENANT_NAME.b2clogin.com',
     realm: 'YOUR_TENANT_NAME.onmicrosoft.com', 
     clientId: 'YOUR_SPA_CLIENT_ID'
   };
   ```

3. **Build & Deploy**:
   ```bash
   npm run build
   ```

---

## 📁 Key Configuration Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/app/auth/keycloak.config.ts` | **Main config** - Switch between Keycloak/Azure AD B2C |
| `src/app/app.config.ts` | Angular providers setup |
| `public/assets/silent-check-sso.html` | Silent SSO support |
| `KEYCLOAK_SETUP.md` | Full documentation |

---

## 🔧 Configuration Variables Location

### Development (Keycloak)
```typescript
// File: src/app/auth/keycloak.config.ts
const keycloakDevConfig: KeycloakConfig = {
  url: 'http://localhost:8090',      // ← Keycloak server
  realm: 'siag-b2c',                 // ← Keycloak realm
  clientId: 'spa-client'             // ← Keycloak client
};
```

### Production (Azure AD B2C)
```typescript
// File: src/app/auth/keycloak.config.ts
const azureAdB2CConfig: KeycloakConfig = {
  url: 'https://your-tenant-name.b2clogin.com',     // ← B2C tenant URL
  realm: 'your-tenant-name.onmicrosoft.com',        // ← B2C tenant name
  clientId: 'your-spa-app-client-id'                // ← B2C app client ID
};
```

---

## 🎯 Switch Configuration

### Current Status Check
Check console logs when app loads:
```
🔐 Authentication Configuration: { environment: 'DEVELOPMENT', provider: 'Keycloak (Local)', ... }
```

### Switch Steps
1. Open `src/app/auth/keycloak.config.ts`
2. Change `const isDevelopment = true;` to `const isDevelopment = false;`
3. Update `azureAdB2CConfig` with your B2C values
4. Rebuild the app

---

## 🔍 Quick Troubleshooting

| Issue | Check |
|-------|-------|
| App won't load | Is Keycloak running on port 8090? |
| Auth fails | Check configuration in keycloak.config.ts |
| Wrong provider | Verify `isDevelopment` flag value |
| Token issues | Check browser console for auth logs |

---

## 📞 Backend API Configuration

### Token Validation
Your backend should validate tokens against:
- **Development**: `http://localhost:8090` (Keycloak)
- **Production**: Your Azure AD B2C tenant URL

### HTTP Interceptor
Tokens automatically added to requests matching:
```typescript
urlPattern: /^(http:\/\/localhost:8080)(\/.*)?$/i
```
Update this pattern in `src/app/app.config.ts` for production API URLs.

---

## ✅ Pre-Deployment Checklist

- [ ] Set `isDevelopment = false`
- [ ] Update all Azure AD B2C config values
- [ ] Test authentication in staging
- [ ] Update API URL patterns if needed
- [ ] Verify CORS settings in Azure AD B2C
- [ ] Test user flows and role assignments
